{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce new offence making AI companies legally liable for AI agent actions",
        "additional_details": "We believe treating illegal acts as being merely 'rogue acts' is simply not good enough they are committed by products that companies have designed & released. These are actions that can potentially have some serious real-world consequences for innocent people and organisations and in our view the AI companies need to be held to account. The government should pass a new law to put beyond doubt that AI companies are criminally responsible for the acts of their AI agents even if they act independently or in unexpected ways. ",
        "background": "AI agents have been found to be involved in several hacking incidents, filing false information with the police & other activities that would be deemed illegal if performed by a human. We call for a new offence making AI companies criminally liable for the independent actions of their AI agents.",
